@Splaktar , @AndrewKushnir , there is a story how I found this bug, may be it will be helpful to understand if we need this PR or not.

I want to be able to declare variable in template. I.e. `<div *myVar="someComponentVar as myTemplateVar">`. To be able to do it I found this code on [stackoverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/a/43172992/3212712)

```
@Directive({
  selector: '[myVar]',
})
export class VarDirective {
  @Input()
  set myVar(context: any) {
    this.context.$implicit = this.context.myVar = context;
    this.updateView();
  }

  context: any = {};

  constructor(private vcRef: ViewContainerRef, private templateRef: TemplateRef<any>) {
  }

  updateView() {
    this.vcRef.clear();
    this.vcRef.createEmbeddedView(this.templateRef, this.context);
  }
}
```

Then, I want to change variable value on some event. So I write this code: `<button (click)="myTemplateVar=someValue">Button</button>`

And it works in dev build. But, if I run `ng build --prod` I get error `ERROR in Cannot assign to a reference or variable!`. So I create question on [stackoverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/57978475/angular-prod-build-error-in-cannot-assign-to-a-reference-or-variable/57979238) about it, as I can't find error cause with so poor error message. In answer I found a place in compiler, which throws error. I tried to fix it by adding one more condition and then everything is working as expected.

So I create 2 PR with changed error message to help developers to found error reason and this with fix. I don't really not if this PR can break something... So, if you think, that it's normal behavior - let's close this PR) But, I'm sure, that in case of closing it, we should merge #32760 with correct error message which can help in finding issue.

If you think, that this PR will not break something I could just remove test, which checks, that error is throwing.

